<title>GERMANY: German third beet test has higher sugar yield.</title>
<headline>German third beet test has higher sugar yield.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The third German sugar beet test of the 1996/97 campaign showed a sugar yield of 7.81 tonnes per hectare compared with 7.66 tonnes in the third test of 1995/96, the sugar industry association WVZ said on Monday.</p>
<p>But the test showed an average sugar content of 15.3 percent compared with 15.5 percent in the third 1995 test and 15.0 percent in the second 1996 test taken a fortnight ago, when the sugar yield was 6.07 tonnes/ha.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
